WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.679
Microsoft Graph and Entra ID run as
separate national cloud deployments,

2
00:00:04.679 --> 00:00:08.700
and a script has to call the hosts
of the cloud its tenant lives in.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:13.725
Commercial and Microsoft 365 GCC
tenants use the same worldwide hosts:

4
00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:18.665
login dot microsoftonline dot com
for sign-in and graph dot microsoft

5
00:00:18.665 --> 00:00:23.350
dot com for Graph, with the Global
environment in Graph PowerShell.

6
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.425
Microsoft's own words are
that a GCC environment

7
00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:29.500
should continue using
the worldwide endpoints.

8
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.252
GCC High and DoD both sign in at
login dot microsoftonline dot U S.

9
00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:39.701
GCC High's Graph host is
graph dot microsoft dot U S,

10
00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:43.825
and DoD's is dod dash graph
dot microsoft dot U S.

11
00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:48.595
In Graph PowerShell those are the U
S Gov and U S Gov DoD environments,

12
00:00:48.595 --> 00:00:53.520
and Azure PowerShell and the Azure
CLI switch to Azure U S Government.
